You are building a Blazor Web App for a recipe sharing community. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-d7bfb3e112f845368d8c6e3f3af85aa1/RecipeShare` using `dotnet new blazor -int Server` (Interactive Server, per-page). 

Program.cs is already correctly configured with `AddInteractiveServerComponents()` and `AddInteractiveServerRenderMode()`. Do NOT modify Program.cs except to register the RecipeService.

## Key Architecture Decisions

- **Per-page interactivity**: Pages are static SSR by default. Only add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to components that need client-side behavior.
- The **homepage**, **category browse page**, and **recipe detail page** are read-only → static SSR (no `@rendermode`).
- The **star rating widget** needs click interactivity → `@rendermode InteractiveServer` on the component.
- The **Submit Recipe form** needs interactivity → `@rendermode InteractiveServer` on the page.
- Use an in-memory service for recipe data (no database).

## Tasks

### 1. Delete default template pages

Delete these files:
- `Components/Pages/Counter.razor`
- `Components/Pages/Weather.razor`
- `Components/Pages/Error.razor` (keep if it exists, it's useful)

### 2. Create AGENTS.md

Create `/tmp/sv-d7bfb3e112f845368d8c6e3f3af85aa1/RecipeShare/AGENTS.md` with this content:

```markdown
# RecipeShare

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| **Interactivity Mode** | Server |
| **Interactivity Scope** | Per-page |

## Rendering configuration
This project uses per-page Interactive Server with prerendering.
Created with `dotnet new blazor -int Server`.

Pages are static SSR by default. Only components that explicitly add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` become interactive.

## Adding new components
- Create new `.razor` files in `Components/Pages/` for routable pages or `Components/` for shared components.
- New pages are static SSR by default. Only add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to components that need client-side behavior.
- Static pages can use standard HTML forms with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` — no interactivity needed.

## Data access
- Components can inject services directly — no HTTP API layer needed.

## Don'ts
- Don't add `@rendermode InteractiveServer` to every page — keep read-only content static for performance.
- Don't set `@rendermode` on `<Routes>` in `App.razor` — that makes it global.
```

### 3. Create Models

Create `/tmp/sv-d7bfb3e112f845368d8c6e3f3af85aa1/RecipeShare/Models/Recipe.cs`:

```csharp
namespace RecipeShare.Models;

public class Recipe
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Category { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public List<string> Ingredients { get; set; } = new();
    public List<string> Steps { get; set; } = new();
    public List<int> Ratings { get; set; } = new();
    public double AverageRating => Ratings.Count > 0 ? Ratings.Average() : 0;
}
```

